WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.970
- [Interviewer] All right, we have Larry,

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.290
Larry Rob, Amanda's father,

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:10.290
and we have Lima who has a
plan in how to help Amanda.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.010
Welcome Lima.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.540
Welcome Larry.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:14.540
- Hello.
- Larry,

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.080
you haven't even seen any of the videos

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.920
I've shot of Amanda, right?

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.920
- No, because after hearing them,

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:21.960
hearing about them I figured,

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.050
well, I had seen the day
to day, the slideshow.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.630
So I'm living it.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.070
So I've not watched the video.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.170
- [Interviewer] No, I recommend you don't.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.640
First off, let me clarify something.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.630
Amanda said some things in
her first interview with me

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:39.883
about you,

00:00:39.883 --> 00:00:44.550
that your oldest daughter
wanted me to clarify

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.890
and make sure everyone understood

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:47.800
they were not true.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.970
Amanda says some crazy things
when she comes in here,

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:52.760
and she says 'em about everybody.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:53.800
So it's not just you.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.430
She said the same thing
about many, many people.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.770
So whatever Amanda said about her father

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:02.880
in that first video,
it's a bunch of nonsense.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.420
So I just wanted to say that.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.200
So Larry, tell me a little
bit about your life.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.220
You have, how many children?

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.130
- I have four children.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.730
I have three girls and one boy.

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:11.730
- [Interviewer] And
Amanda is your youngest.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.940
- Amanda is my youngest child.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:14.820
- [Interviewer] And
tell me about your life.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.490
You were a war veteran.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.430
- Yes, I went into the air force.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.530
I had some scholarships
offered out of high school,

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:24.850
but I chose to do a university
and it was quite expensive,

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:28.050
so I chose the air force
'cause I wanted to travel.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:29.360
So after choosing that then

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:32.490
all sort of opportunities opened up.

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:35.580
I was kind of a young guy
having fun, going around.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.110
Had some good deployments.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.833
The air force was very good to me.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.860
I did 11 and a half years there.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.930
So, travel and all of that sort of

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:48.280
fill those young man
intuitions have something to do

00:01:49.158 --> 00:01:50.230
that was beyond me.

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:53.120
So that was an experience
I'll never, never forget.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:56.970
And I'm still having benefits
from it 45 years later.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:58.093
- [Interviewer] That's great.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:01.080
So the issues with
Amanda had been going on

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.490
for about how long?

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:05.136
- Since September of 2016.

00:02:05.136 --> 00:02:06.640
- [Interviewer] How did it start?

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.120
She was in college, right?

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.000
- Yeah, she and I.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.830
She was at the CSUN, Cal State Northridge.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:15.910
She had had a successful
elementary and high school.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:17.930
She went to a chartered
high school because

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:19.990
as a single parent, I say, well,

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.780
let me just do whatever I
can to fill in the blank.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:26.240
Give her that extra edge for, projectory,

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:27.073
trajectory.

00:02:27.073 --> 00:02:30.490
So she did very, very well in high school.

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.970
And she went to CSUN.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:33.980
She was doing very well.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:36.080
She was a critical thinker, a writer.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.800
So she was doing well in her classes.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.900
But then she started to not show up

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:42.553
when I would visit her during the mid week

00:02:42.553 --> 00:02:44.203
to take her her groceries.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:47.500
I was at the university myself.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.480
She challenged me.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.140
So I said, okay, I went into Domingus.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:52.480
So that's why I was at the university

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.260
because she challenged me.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:57.030
So I went to get a degree
in sociology at that time,

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.690
but I was going up there
as a parent twice a week,

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.270
and she would disappear.

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:04.340
And then she started to tell me

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.720
that she was being surveilled.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:06.760
And I said, "Oh no,"

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.854
I'm thinking from my military days,

00:03:08.854 --> 00:03:10.897
I said, "they don't
even have the resources

00:03:10.897 --> 00:03:12.470
"to keep up with you, Amanda Bear."

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.440
So that's kinda how this started.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.930
And then after a few
months of not seeing her,

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.630
she had established some new
friends that I never met,

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:26.380
I had her diagnosed and it
was schizophrenia bipolar.

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:30.107
And that was September of 2016.

00:03:30.107 --> 00:03:31.800
- [Interviewer] And then she
started using crack, right?

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.720
- She started using crack.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.380
That was the following year.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.010
First when she started,

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:38.810
she started using meth.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:39.870
Meth scared her.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:42.070
In counseling she said, "Oh my gosh."

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:45.110
She looked at me in a way
that I knew she was sincere.

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:46.740
She said, no, meth scared her.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.540
So she stopped using meth

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.250
after the first six, seven, eight months.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.360
This is from looking back on it,

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.440
because at the time I didn't
know she was using drugs.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:59.280
So she was starting to
talk about using crack.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.160
So she began to use crack in 2017.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.740
So she's been using crack.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.993
She had used meth a couple times,

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.100
from time to time,

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.500
but she's been using,

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.550
I mean cocaine since then.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.540
- [Interviewer] So you
and I have been struggling

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:18.400
with Amanda all of this
year and some of last year.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.297
- Every day,

00:04:19.297 --> 00:04:20.130
every day.
- But you've been

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:20.963
on the front lines.

00:04:20.963 --> 00:04:21.796
You're her father.

00:04:21.796 --> 00:04:24.710
So you've been seeing it from the start.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:27.200
But you've seen some crazy,
crazy behavior, right?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.100
I mean, Amanda jumps out of cars.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.020
She gets beaten up.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.970
She walks around through the night.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:34.630
- The extreme.
- Barefoot?

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:36.380
- Oh, the extreme.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.110
First, the first year and a half or so

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:40.780
she was down in LA,

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:44.590
Florence, Western, Vermont,
Manchester, those areas.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.070
So it was quite different for me

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:47.470
because I had to go there

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:48.960
just to catch up with her every day.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:50.400
So that's what I did.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.470
I put it on my agenda.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:52.783
Everyday I would go there.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:02.640
So I had not seen her for
like three or four days.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:06.437
So I was gonna go to 77th and
make an MIA, missing person.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:12.363
I was already, she was on
the front seat of the bus.

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:15.463
I got onto the bus.

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:18.220
I didn't recognize her.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:19.833
So I went on and sat down.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:24.240
After a stop or so she came back to me,

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:27.813
and that different person
that I saw, I didn't know.

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:30.823
She was right in front of my face.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.330
I felt so bad.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:36.410
To this day I felt so bad

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:38.460
because I didn't know her at first.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.800
So after I recognized her,
she just looked up at me

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.420
and talked to me the way she always does.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:44.253
She said, "Dad."

00:05:44.253 --> 00:05:45.910
I said, "Honey, what you need?"

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.357
So I said, "Let's go get you some,

00:05:47.357 --> 00:05:48.577
"get you an outfit."

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:51.493
So we did that.

00:05:53.404 --> 00:05:54.830
She just wanted to smoke.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.100
After we got her outfit, got
her shoes and everything,

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.700
she looked so nice.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:02.477
She just said to me,
she say, "I'm thirsty.

00:06:02.477 --> 00:06:03.740
"I just wanna go smoke."

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:06.590
So it took me a half hour.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.933
So I walked up and down
Manchester with her.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:14.970
So, I let her go and smoke.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:17.150
So after that, it was day to day.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.730
And then she disappeared on me.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:20.563
I did MIA,

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:22.526
and they found her.

00:06:22.526 --> 00:06:23.670
She was in the hospital.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:24.503
Thank God.

00:06:24.503 --> 00:06:27.250
And I was trying to do a conservatorship,

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.550
but I didn't have my ducks in line.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:30.883
So they released her.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:34.450
So I didn't see her for awhile.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:37.823
And the VA moved me downtown
for a section eight housing.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.020
So I didn't see her.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:42.880
And I, I'm sorry.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:45.247
- [Interviewer] What was Amanda
like before this happened?

00:06:45.247 --> 00:06:47.610
- She was just such a,

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:49.570
she was almost eloquent to me.

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:53.130
She was always, "Yes dad,
please dad, excuse me dad."

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:55.600
And I just did every, I
kinda relive my childhood.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.940
So she got everything she really wanted.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:03.260
Disneyland, Knotts Berry,
all that every year.

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:05.010
Come on, Dodger Stadium.

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.660
I think I was more on the hot dogs and...

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:08.570
You know what I'm saying.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.130
She had a good childhood.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.810
All the concerts I could get her into.

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:15.010
And Nikia.

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:16.060
And you know what I'm saying?

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.810
As long as the parent could
take them, I took her.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:21.220
So she had a good childhood.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:23.230
She was having a good
time at the university.

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:26.180
It's just a set of friends I never met.

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:28.270
And I was almost certain
that there was something

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:31.900
in that relationship
that caused her to stray.

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:35.320
So after day to day down
there, I didn't see her.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.340
And I was coming in from church one Sunday

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:39.730
and I saw Amanda downtown,

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.940
and she saw me, and it was such a relief.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.550
And then I had been
helping her and I met Mark.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:46.980
And every day it's the challenge.

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:47.813
It's different.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:49.483
It's just-

00:07:49.483 --> 00:07:51.480
- [Interviewer] One day
she disappeared for a week.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:52.530
One day she-

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.880
- She'd been ran over by a car.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:58.303
She had all her lower and
upper teeth knocked out.

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:02.650
She's just challenging
because of her behavior now.

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:07.290
She only feels like the
drug gives her relief.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.150
- [Interviewer] There's absolutely
no way to stop this girl

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:10.950
from getting the drugs she wants.

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:11.860
- No.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.900
- [Interviewer] There
was one time that I was,

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:16.260
you might remember, I was
trying to take her to the clinic

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:19.217
to get the prescription
for her schizophrenia,

00:08:19.217 --> 00:08:20.960
for the medication she needs.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:23.480
And as soon as she figured out that I

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:25.410
wasn't taking her to my studio,

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:27.430
she backs her legs up and start,

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:29.000
she was gonna kick the
windows out of my car

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.664
to get out of a moving vehicle.

00:08:30.664 --> 00:08:31.497
(laughing)

00:08:31.497 --> 00:08:33.110
So I had to let her out.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.580
- She'll bolt.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:35.700
No, she'll bolt.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:36.930
She'll bolt, she's done that.

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:38.220
- [Interviewer] Yeah,
she'll jump out of the car.

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:40.350
- She's been injured three or four times

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.380
because she jumps out of cars.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:45.930
She's lost her sense
of defense and danger.

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:48.280
Danger, danger, stranger, stranger.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:50.500
She and I, she never had to engage

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.010
with strange people as a child,

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.460
from daycare to school.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:56.630
You know what I mean.

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:59.250
So now it's just totally different.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:00.837
She's walkin' around Skid Row.

00:09:00.837 --> 00:09:02.390
- Barefoot.
- Barefoot.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:04.367
Sometimes come in-
- No pants on.

00:09:04.367 --> 00:09:05.200
- No clothes.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:06.320
I've given her outfit.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:07.153
'Cause that's what I do.

00:09:07.153 --> 00:09:09.277
Every day I go out, I get her something.

00:09:09.277 --> 00:09:10.480
'Cause you gotta have some pants.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:12.510
Mark has given her clothes.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:16.960
So she was just no longer
in control of her behavior.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:20.560
She no longer had a sense
of, okay, this is respectful.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:21.520
This is harmful.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:23.480
This is not good.

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:26.120
- And Larry, you and I speak
on the phone very often.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.240
- Very often.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:28.550
- [Interviewer] And so
many times we've said

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:31.120
we just need a miracle,
'cause nothing is happening.

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:32.243
- We had to have one.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.290
- [Interviewer] And nothing seems to work.

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:37.300
The 5150s, the cops pick her up,

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.800
and they just let her go right away.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:42.140
- And then the difference
maker is she assaulted me,

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:44.342
because I was cooperative.

00:09:44.342 --> 00:09:46.270
I was glad to know that I could help her

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.760
manage her benefits every month

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.280
so she don't just run out in a few days.

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:53.500
But after she assaulted
me the second time,

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:56.480
I said I have to do something differently.

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:00.440
And then we got a call
from Mark about Lima.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:03.360
And when I heard about
someone that may help us...

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:06.580
At the time I had some
of the professionals

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:10.270
in the mental health field
here in LA trying to help me.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:13.080
But all they were doing was counseling me.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:15.460
Amanda was comin' in and
out of that door every day,

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:16.873
creating a problem.

00:10:16.873 --> 00:10:18.630
- [Interviewer] One of my friends is a,

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:21.247
is like the head of the West Side of LA's

00:10:22.284 --> 00:10:26.330
AA, NA groups, all the addiction groups.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:29.010
And he, I was telling him about Amanda.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:30.270
And he said with people like that,

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:31.830
there's nothing you can do.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:33.628
You just have to let 'em go.

00:10:33.628 --> 00:10:35.210
You can't stop them.

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:37.010
There's no helping them.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:38.830
- So this is a miracle.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:40.663
'Cause I've seen that day to day.

00:10:41.516 --> 00:10:45.197
And I thank you, Mark, for
introducing me to Lima and Ivan.

00:10:45.197 --> 00:10:46.810
What a blessing.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:49.530
- [Interviewer] Yeah, and
then along comes Lima.

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:51.030
So let me explain what you do.

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:55.530
